<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (At B1 level, you can understand and use everyday language quite well. You should know words that help you talk about things like family, work and hobbies. You'll also start to use more adjectives and adverbs to make your sentences interesting. Knowing more words helps you feel more confident when you speak or write in English. It also makes it easier for you to understand what people are saying or what you're reading. In this section, we show you some of the common topics you should be able to speak about freely as a B1 student.)
/E (At B1 level, you can understand and use everyday language quite well. You should know words that help you talk about things like family, work and hobbies. You'll also start to use more adjectives and adverbs to make your sentences interesting. Knowing more words helps you feel more confident when you speak or write in English. It also makes it easier for you to understand what people are saying or what you're reading. In this section, we show you some of the common topics you should be able to speak about freely as a B1 student.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
